meta {
  name: Create Product List
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/pim-product-lists
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
  Content-Type: application/json
  Accept: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "name": "WC Test Static List",
    "type": "Static"
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 201
  res.body.data.type: eq Static
}

docs {
  Confirmed live 2026-09-08 against "David's Dev Account". **Fixture
  kept** -- id `6aa025bd2b6fd055ffb7cab4`, for Channels/Ecatalogs (Phase
  4) to reference via `product_list_id`.

  `201 Created`.

  ## Major finding -- how "Static" list membership actually works
  Neither `ProductListCreateInputDto` nor the create response has any
  field for a fixed member-ID array (`product_ids` etc. don't exist).
  Instead, creating a `type: "Static"` list **auto-generates a `query`**
  targeting the list's own id:
  `[[{"operator":"in","field":"static_lists","value":["<this list's own
  id>"],"field_type":"PimProductAttribute.ObjectIdAttribute"}]]`. So a
  Static list is really just a Smart list whose query is
  `static_lists contains <list_id>` -- membership isn't stored on the
  list at all, it's stored on **each product's own `static_list_ids`
  field**. To add a product to this list, `PATCH /products/{id}` with
  `{"static_list_ids": ["6aa025bd2b6fd055ffb7cab4"]}` -- confirmed working
  (see `02-Products-v3`'s kept product, which now has this list linked;
  verify via `GET /products/{id}/static_lists`, a computed subpath, not
  via `_fields=static_list_ids` on the main resource, which is silently
  dropped like other relationship-array fields in this API).

  ## Not idempotent to re-run
  List names are unique per account. Re-running once the fixture exists
  returns `422 {"errors":[{"name":"ValidationError","description":"A
  List with same name already exists"}]}` -- expected, not a bug
  (`config/api-testing.config.md` quirk #38a).

  ## Smart list (absorbed from "Create Smart Product List.bru")
  Confirmed live 2026-09-08. **Fixture kept** -- id
  `6aa0322d2b6fd055ffb7cabb`, for Phase 4 via `product_list_id`.
  `query` is a nested array-of-arrays of filter objects
  (`operator`/`field`/`value`/`field_type`) -- matches
  `ProductRelationshipAggregationFilterModel`/`FilterModel`'s shape in
  the spec. Filters directly on `sku`, matching the kept product from
  Phase 2b (`WC-TEST-FULL-001`). Not idempotent to re-run once the
  fixture exists -- same `422` duplicate-name behavior.

  Confirmed live 2026-09-21: new smart list created with id
  `6ab19d713e4f2e9945fdf718` ("WC Test Smart List 2026-09-21"),
  `query: [[{"operator":"like","field":"sku","value":"WC"}]]`. Valid
  operators for Smart list `query` include: `exists`, `like`, `eq`, `gt`,
  `gte`, `lt`, `lte`, `!exists`, `!like`, `!eq`, `in`, `!in`,
  `text_search`, `last_days`, etc. The operator `icontains` is **NOT
  valid** for stored queries (it is valid for live query-string filters
  on search endpoints -- these are two different filter DSLs).

  ## 422 -- missing required fields (absorbed from "Create Product List - Missing Fields (422).bru")
  Confirmed live 2026-09-08. Empty body `{}` returns 422 with **two**
  entries in `errors` (one per missing required field -- `name` and
  `type` both required). First time this project has seen multiple entries
  in the `errors` array at once; still the same flat `{name, description}`
  envelope shape as every other 422 confirmed so far.
}

example {
  name: 201 - Success (Smart List)
  description: Confirmed live 2026-09-08 and 2026-09-21. query is a nested array-of-arrays of filter objects; valid operators include like, eq, in, exists, etc. (not icontains).

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/pim-product-lists
    method: post
    mode: json
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Content-Type: application/json
      Accept: application/json
    }
    body:json: {
      {
        "name": "WC Test Smart List",
        "type": "Smart",
        "query": [[{"operator": "eq", "field": "sku", "value": "WC-TEST-FULL-001"}]]
      }
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 201
      text: Created
    }
    headers: {
      content-type: application/json; charset=utf-8
    }
    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "data": {
            "id": "6ab19d713e4f2e9945fdf718",
            "account_id": "6a38f5a5b22478f30bfd755c",
            "name": "WC Test Smart List 2026-09-21",
            "type": "Smart",
            "query": [
              [
                {
                  "operator": "like",
                  "field": "sku",
                  "value": "WC",
                  "field_type": null
                }
              ]
            ],
            "created": "2026-09-21T21:11:13.986497+00:00",
            "modified": "2026-09-21T21:11:14.000299+00:00"
          },
          "errors": []
        }
      '''
    }
  }
}

example {
  name: 201 - Full Parameters (Multi-Group Query)
  description: Confirmed live 2026-09-22 against a disposable scratch Smart list (id 6ab2fa2c125f1d0ceeeed6b4, deleted after capture). ProductListCreateInputDto only has name/type/query fields, so "full parameters" means exercising query's full expressiveness -- outer array is OR-ed groups, inner array is AND-ed conditions within a group. This example combines two AND conditions in the first group with a second OR-ed group, across three different operators (eq, gt, like).

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/pim-product-lists
    method: post
    mode: json
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Content-Type: application/json
      Accept: application/json
    }
    body:json: {
      {
        "name": "WC Test Full Params Smart List",
        "type": "Smart",
        "query": [
          [
            {"operator": "eq", "field": "status", "value": "Completed"},
            {"operator": "gt", "field": "attributes.amazon_ready", "value": 50}
          ],
          [
            {"operator": "like", "field": "sku", "value": "WC"}
          ]
        ]
      }
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 201
      text: Created
    }
    headers: {
      content-type: application/json; charset=utf-8
    }
    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "data": {
            "id": "6ab2fa2c125f1d0ceeeed6b4",
            "account_id": "6a38f5a5b22478f30bfd755c",
            "name": "WC Test Full Params Smart List",
            "query": [
              [
                {"operator": "eq", "field": "status", "value": "Completed", "field_type": null},
                {"operator": "gt", "field": "attributes.amazon_ready", "value": 50, "field_type": null}
              ],
              [
                {"operator": "like", "field": "sku", "value": "WC", "field_type": null}
              ]
            ],
            "created": "2026-09-22T21:59:08.221838+00:00",
            "modified": "2026-09-22T21:59:08.233651+00:00",
            "type": "Smart"
          },
          "errors": []
        }
      '''
    }
  }
}

example {
  name: 422 - Missing Required Fields (name, type)
  description: Confirmed live 2026-09-08. Both name and type are required; missing either returns 422 with one errors entry per missing field.

  request: {
    url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/pim-product-lists
    method: post
    mode: json
    headers: {
      Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
      Content-Type: application/json
      Accept: application/json
    }
    body:json: {
      {}
    }
  }

  response: {
    status: {
      code: 422
      text: Unprocessable Entity
    }
    headers: {
      content-type: application/json; charset=utf-8
    }
    body: {
      type: json
      content: '''
        {
          "data": [],
          "errors": [
            {
              "name": "InputDTOValidationError",
              "description": "name: Field required"
            },
            {
              "name": "InputDTOValidationError",
              "description": "type: Field required"
            }
          ]
        }
      '''
    }
  }
}
